The ground lemma cannot preempt the supplied `[concrete]` function evaluator, so the float connection still crashes before simplification. I’m removing that failed extension and changing the source comparison to the Python-equivalent `x > 0.0`. This avoids any ground `Int2Float(0)` call: both Int and Float paths now execute the frozen mixed-float comparison rules symbolically, allowing a genuinely bridge-free connection theorem.
